{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-18-1","title":"Luke 18:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Of the importunate widow. 9 Of the Pharisee and the publican. 15 Of Children brought to Christ. 18 A ruler would follow Christ, but is hindered by his riches. 28 The reward of them that leave all for his sake. 31 He foretells his death; 35 and restores a blind man to his sight.</p>\n<p>that. 11:5-8; 21:36; Ge 32:9-12,24-26; Job 27:8-10; Ps 55:16,17; 65:2 Ps 86:3; *marg: Ps 102:17; 142:5-7; Jer 29:12; Ro 12:12; Eph 6:18; Php 4:6 Col 4:2,12; 1Th 5:17 and not. Ps 27:13; Jon 2:7; Ga 6:9; Heb 12:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-18-2","title":"Luke 18:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>city. Gr. certain city. which. 4; Ex 18:21,22; 2Ch 19:3-9; Job 29:7-17; Ps 8:1-4; Jer 22:16,17 Eze 22:6-8; Mic 3:1-3; Ro 3:14-18 regarded. Pr 29:7; Isa 33:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-18-3","title":"Luke 18:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>a widow. De 27:19; 2Sa 14:5-24; Job 22:9; 29:13; Isa 1:17,21-23; Jer 5:28 Avenge. 7,8; Ro 13:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-18-4","title":"Luke 18:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>he said. 12:17; 16:3; Heb 4:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-18-5","title":"Luke 18:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>because. 11:8; Jud 16:16; 2Sa 13:24-27 weary. 39; Mt 15:23; Mr 10:47,48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-18-7","title":"Luke 18:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>shall. 11:13; Mt 7:11 avenge. 1Sa 